        "raw": "<p>Those are *excellent* questions!</p><blockquote><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: &quot;Open Sans&quot;, HelveticaNeue, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">What happens if you use Entwined Power to gift Absorb Essence to a different spirit?</span></p></blockquote><p>You follow as much of the instructions as you can:</p><ul><li><strong>Gain 3 Energy</strong> - you can do this, so you do.</li><li><strong>Move 1 of target Spirit&#39;s Presence to your &quot;Deep Slumber&quot; track</strong> - you can&#39;t do this, because you don&#39;t have a Deep Slumber track.</li><li><strong>Absorbed Presence cannot be returned to play</strong> - you didn&#39;t Absorb any, so this is irrelevant.*</li><li><strong>Target Spirit gains Any Element and 1 Energy</strong> - you can do this, so you do.</li></ul><p>So the net effect is &quot;Gain 3 Energy. Target Spirit gains Any Element and 1 Energy.&quot;</p><p><em>* = The term &quot;Absorbed Presence&quot; isn&#39;t formally defined anywhere, but everybody understands what it means.</em></p><blockquote><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: &quot;Open Sans&quot;, HelveticaNeue, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Also, what about Ocean&#39;s power cards that drown Invaders?</span></p></blockquote><p>Ocean&#39;s Special Rules define what &quot;Drown&quot; means: &quot;Destroy Drowned pieces, placing Drowned Invaders here <em>[on Ocean&#39;s playmat]</em>.&quot; So if another player Drowns an Invader, it goes onto Ocean&#39;s playmat as usual.</p><p>It is, however, ambiguous whether it&#39;s Ocean or the other Spirit which actually performs the destruction, which while rarely relevant has the potential to be <em>(eg, if the other Spirit is Bringer of Dreams and Nightmares)</em>. I&#39;ll need to think on that, but I suspect it&#39;s the Power-using Spirit which performs the Destruction. (And that the last sentence of &quot;Ocean in Play&quot; ought to be reworded as &quot;You Drown any Invaders or [Dahan] moved to those Oceans.&quot; to make it clear that it&#39;s Ocean who&#39;s doing the Drowning in those cases.)</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
